  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "tbP = 67108859;\ntbModP[tbx_] := Mod[Numerator[tbx] PowerMod[Denominator[tbx], -1, tbP], tbP];\ntbY8 = ArrayReshape[Map[tbModP, Normal[tbY], {2}], {4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4}];\ntbCuts = {{\"sites {1,2} | {3,4}\", {1, 2, 5, 6}}, {\"site 1 | {2,3,4}\", {1, 5}}, {\"site 2 | {1,3,4}\", {2, 6}}, {\"site 3 | {1,2,4}\", {3, 7}}, {\"site 4 | {1,2,3}\", {4, 8}}, {\"sites {1,3} | {2,4}\", {1, 3, 5, 7}}};\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{tbcut[[1]], MatrixRank[Flatten[tbY8, {tbcut[[2]], Complement[Range[8], tbcut[[2]]]}], Modulus -> tbP], Min[4^Length[tbcut[[2]]], 4^(8 - Length[tbcut[[2]]])]}, {tbcut, tbCuts}], {\"cut\", \"operator-Schmidt rank of Y (mod p)\", \"maximal possible\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result of the cell above (python port, exact mod p = 67108859; not yet run in Wolfram).**\n\n| cut | operator-Schmidt rank of Y | maximal possible |\n|---|---|---|\n| sites {1,2} \\| {3,4} | 169 | 256 |\n| site 1 \\| {2,3,4} | 13 | 16 |\n| site 2 \\| {1,3,4} | 16 | 16 |\n| site 3 \\| {1,2,4} | 16 | 16 |\n| site 4 \\| {1,2,3} | 13 | 16 |\n| sites {1,3} \\| {2,4} | 201 | 256 |\n\n(The word matrix M has the same ranks across these cuts where checked: 169, 13, 13.) Y is far from factorised between the two blocks, so two-block bras have no factorised SoV expansion in general (16×16 rank 16 in the table above); low rank only occurs when one block is at (or close to) the SoV vacuum.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 6. Parameter fixing: which two-block rotations of ⟨0| give the physical bra\n\n**Target.** C₀(Ψ₀) = ⟨vac⊗W₋₁|Ψ₀⟩ = ⟨W₋₁⊗vac|Ψ₀⟩ (cyclic states), W_a = (e₁+ae₄)⊗(e₄−ae₁), diagonal frame. For untwisted highest-weight Ψ₀, ⟨Bρ(n)|Ψ₀⟩ = ⟨B|Ψ₀⟩ for upper-unitriangular n; the torus D acts by the character D^{wt} (exactly, also on twisted states, which have definite weight in the diagonal frame).\n\n**The SoV vacuum is itself in the HW orbit of the physical vacuum.** In the diagonal frame ⟨0| = (λ⊗𝟙)^{⊗2}, λ_j = 1/∏_{m≠j}(z_j−z_m) (Lagrange weights; 𝟙 = (1,1,1,1)), and with r = λ/λ₁\n\n⟨0| = λ₁²·(vac⊗vac)·ρ(n'D'), n' = ((1,1,1,r₄),(0,1,0,−r₂),(0,0,1,−r₃),(0,0,0,1)), D' = diag(1, r₂, r₃, 1).\n\nn' and D' have **finite limits** as z = 1+εφ → 1 (r_j are ratios of twist differences, depending only on the direction φ — the analogue of 2603's finite polarisation ratios).\n\n**Two-block rotations.** Since n'D'E₁₄(n'D')⁻¹ = E₁₄ (n' upper unitriangular, d'₁ = d'₄ = 1), the general block rotations with ⟨0|ρ₁₂(g₁)ρ₃₄(g₂) ∝ (W₋₁⊗vac)ρ(m) (m Borel×torus, diagonal frame) are g₁ = s₁(1 + b𝔼)μ, g₂ = s₂(1 + b'𝔼)μ with s_i in the (n'D'-conjugated) stabilisers of the pair lines, μ a common Borel factor (invisible on HW states) and **𝔼 = E₁₄ in the twist eigenbasis** (diagonal frame); dropping s_i, μ:\n\n⟨0|ρ₁₂(1+b𝔼)ρ₃₄(1+b'𝔼) = λ₁²(W_b⊗W_{b'})ρ(n'D'),  ⟨…|Ψ₀⟩ = λ₁² (b'−b)^{2−w₁} C₀(Ψ₀)\n\nfor HW Ψ₀ of weight (w₁,0,0,−w₁) (every state with C ≠ 0 has w₂ = w₃ = 0; the HW shift e^{cE₁₄} moves (a,a') → (a+c,a'+c)). The only fixed datum is b' − b ≠ 0; the **sparsest choice is b' = 0** (block 2 = SoV vacuum). In the companion frame 𝔼 acts on A sites by v ↦ (v·ℓ₁)v_{z₄} and on F sites (as −𝔼ᵀ) by u ↦ −(u·v_{z₄})ℓ₁ (ℓ₁ = row 1 of V⁻¹ = coefficients of the Lagrange polynomial of z₁, v_{z₄} = (z₄³,z₄²,z₄,1)), so\n\nB(b) := ⟨0|ρ₁₂(1+b𝔼) = (e₁ + bλ₁v_{z₄}) ⊗ (e₄ − bℓ₁) ⊗ e₁ ⊗ e₄ (companion frame),\n\ni.e. pair 1 carries the cubic twist polynomials v_{z₄} = e₁∏_{m≠4}(G_cᵀ−z_m) and ℓ₁ = λ₁e₄∏_{m≠1}(G_c−z_m) (the physical vacuum needs degree-3 Lagrange projectors). Note 1 + b𝔼 is not a twist polynomial (it is off-diagonal in the twist eigenbasis) — which is why no localising word produces it. In the untwisting limit take b fixed (b ↔ 2603's κ-dependent ratio): B(b)/λ₁² → (W_b⊗vac)ρ(n'₀D'₀) has a finite limit, so ⟨B(b)|Ψ_ε⟩/(λ₁²(−b)^{2−w₁}) → C₀. Code: exact checks of both decompositions (symbolic b, b') and the SoV expansion of B(b).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "tbLam[tbz_] := Table[1/Product[If[tbm == tbj, 1, tbz[[tbj]] - tbz[[tbm]]], {tbm, 4}], {tbj, 4}];\ntbRho4[tbvs_, tbg_] := Table[If[tbTypes[[tbs]] == \"A\", tbvs[[tbs]] . tbg, tbvs[[tbs]] . Transpose[Inverse[tbg]]], {tbs, 4}];\ntbWpair[tba_] := {tbU[1] + tba tbU[4], tbU[4] - tba tbU[1]};\ntbBdiag[tbb_, tbbp_, tbz_] := With[{l = tbLam[tbz], one = {1, 1, 1, 1}}, tbKet[{l + tbb l[[1]] tbU[4], one - tbb tbU[1], l + tbbp l[[1]] tbU[4], one - tbbp tbU[1]}]];\ntbNp[tbz_] := With[{r = tbLam[tbz]/tbLam[tbz][[1]]}, {{1, 1, 1, r[[4]]}, {0, 1, 0, -r[[2]]}, {0, 0, 1, -r[[3]]}, {0, 0, 0, 1}}];\ntbDp[tbz_] := With[{r = tbLam[tbz]/tbLam[tbz][[1]]}, DiagonalMatrix[{1, r[[2]], r[[3]], 1}]];\ntbVz4[tbz_] := tbVand[tbz][[All, 4]]; tbL1[tbz_] := Inverse[tbVand[tbz]][[1]];\ntbRinv[tbz_] := With[{V = tbVand[tbz]}, KroneckerProduct[Transpose[V], Inverse[V], Transpose[V], Inverse[V]]];\ntbBcomp[tbb_, tbbp_, tbz_] := With[{l1 = tbLam[tbz][[1]]}, tbKet[{tbU[1] + tbb l1 tbVz4[tbz], tbU[4] - tbb tbL1[tbz], tbU[1] + tbbp l1 tbVz4[tbz], tbU[4] - tbbp tbL1[tbz]}]];\nClear[tbbb, tbbbp];\ntbDecompOK = Union[Expand[tbKet[tbRho4[Join[tbWpair[tbbb], tbWpair[tbbbp]], tbNp[tbZ0] . tbDp[tbZ0]]] - tbBdiag[tbbb, tbbbp, tbZ0]/tbLam[tbZ0][[1]]^2]] === {0};\ntbVacOK = tbKet[{tbLam[tbZ0], {1, 1, 1, 1}, tbLam[tbZ0], {1, 1, 1, 1}}] . tbRinv[tbZ0] == tbVac;\ntbFrameOK = Union[Expand[tbBcomp[tbbb, tbbbp, tbZ0] . tbRmat[tbZ0] - tbBdiag[tbbb, tbbbp, tbZ0]]] === {0};\ntbCb = Expand[Normal[tbBcomp[tbbb, 0, tbZ0] . tbY]];\ntbCpieces = Table[Coefficient[tbCb, tbbb, tbk], {tbk, 0, 2}];\ntbSupp = Flatten[Position[tbCb, Except[0], {1}, Heads -> False]];\ntbSuppL = tbLabels[[tbSupp]];\nGrid[{{\"⟨0| (diag) = (λ⊗𝟙)^⊗2 maps to the companion SoV vacuum\", tbVacOK},\n  {\"(W_b⊗W_b')ρ(n'D') = ⟨0|ρ₁₂(1+b𝔼)ρ₃₄(1+b'𝔼)/λ₁² (symbolic b, b', exact)\", tbDecompOK},\n  {\"companion form of the bra = diag form · R⁻¹ (symbolic b, b')\", tbFrameOK},\n  {\"n', D' at z₀\", Row[{MatrixForm[tbNp[tbZ0]], \"  \", MatrixForm[tbDp[tbZ0]]}]},\n  {\"B(b) = ⟨0|ρ₁₂(1+b𝔼): # SoV words\", Length[tbSupp]},\n  {\"  values of a₃ / k₄ used\", {Union[tbSuppL[[All, 3]]], Union[tbSuppL[[All, 4]]]}},\n  {\"  # words in the b⁰, b¹, b² pieces\", Count[#, Except[0]] & /@ tbCpieces},\n  {\"  b⁰ piece\", tbCpieces[[1]] == UnitVector[256, 1]},\n  {\"two-block B(b,b') with b,b' ≠ 0: # SoV words\", Count[Normal[tbBcomp[3/7, -2/5, tbZ0] . tbY], Except[0]]},\n  {\"global (b = b'): # SoV words\", Count[Normal[tbBcomp[3/7, 3/7, tbZ0] . tbY], Except[0]]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result of the cell above (python port: sympy exact with symbolic b, b'; mod-p exact counts; not yet run in Wolfram).**\n\n| check | result |\n|---|---|\n| ⟨0| (diag) = (λ⊗𝟙)^⊗2 maps to the companion SoV vacuum (λVᵀ = e₁, 𝟙V⁻¹ = e₄) | True |\n| (W_b⊗W_b')ρ(n'D') = ⟨0|ρ₁₂(1+b𝔼)ρ₃₄(1+b'𝔼)/λ₁² (symbolic b, b') | True |\n| companion form of the bra = diag form · R⁻¹ (per site, symbolic b) | True |\n| n', D' at z₀ | n' = ((1,1,1,−245/76),(0,1,0,260/133),(0,0,1,−117/28),(0,0,0,1)), D' = diag(1, −260/133, 117/28, 1) |\n| B(b) = ⟨0|ρ₁₂(1+b𝔼): # SoV words | 36 |\n| values of a₃ / k₄ used | {0} / {0,1,2} |\n| # words in the b⁰, b¹, b² pieces | 1, 17, 36 |\n| b⁰ piece = ⟨0| | True |\n| two-block B(3/7, −2/5): # SoV words | 256 |\n| global (b = b' = 3/7): # SoV words | 256 |\n\nAlso checked (python, exact mod p): v_{z₄} = e₁∏_{m≠4}(G_cᵀ−z_m) and ℓ₁ = λ₁ e₄∏_{m≠1}(G_c−z_m) — pair 1 of B(b) carries cubic twist polynomials.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
