   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 9. Summary (2026-10-12; all numbers from python, the Wolfram cells are unrun — see the status note at the top)\n\n**Setup [exact mod p].** t₁, t₂, t₃ from quantum minors commute; calibration (i) c₁ = 603680/25947 reproduced on **global** BPS rotations (it fails on two-block states: end-site localisation needs a global reference); (ii) twisted-vacuum eigenbra exact. Word basis: rank 256, exactly z-independent, **block diagonal in the SoV charge** |x| = a₁+k₂+a₃+k₄ = Σ(A: i−1, F: 4−j) (blocks 1,4,10,20,31,40,44,40,31,20,10,4,1; 2929 nonzeros in M and in M⁻¹), so the dual basis is exact and cheap. ⟨x|Ψ⟩ = W(x)⟨0|Ψ⟩ on all 256 twisted states [float, 3·10⁻⁹].\n\n**Coefficient structure [exact mod p].** c_x(B) = (B·M⁻¹)_x; operator-Schmidt rank of M⁻¹ across {1,2}|{3,4} is 169 (of 256), 13 at the end sites: two-block bras do not factorise in general (16×16 rank 16). Left block cheap, right block expensive: generic block {1,2} with block {3,4} at the SoV vacuum → 36 words (a₃ = 0, k₄ ≤ 2, pair-cut rank 3); block {3,4} generic → 130; {4,1} → 96; {2,3} → 83. Companion flags (= Lagrange-weighted twist-adapted vectors) are the sparse families (table §5).\n\n**Parameter fixing [exact (sympy, mod p) + 60d/90d].** ⟨0| is itself a finite (z → 1) Borel×torus rotation of the physical vacuum: ⟨0| = λ₁²(vac⊗vac)ρ(n'D'). The block rotations that give the physical bra are g₁ = 1+b𝔼, g₂ = 1+b'𝔼 (up to stabilisers and a common Borel factor), 𝔼 = E₁₄ in the twist eigenbasis (not a twist polynomial), with ⟨0|ρ₁₂(g₁)ρ₃₄(g₂)|Ψ₀⟩ = λ₁²(b'−b)^{2−w₁}C₀. Sparsest: b' = 0, B(b) = (e₁+bλ₁v_{z₄})⊗(e₄−bℓ₁)⊗e₁⊗e₄, 36 SoV words, b-pieces 1/17/36 words, seen in the limit by vacuum/adjoint/singlet. Untwisting with the saved L = 2 HW states (z = 1+εφ, θ = θ_ABJM+εθ⁰, ε = 10⁻²,10⁻³,10⁻⁴): C_pred → data C₂ linearly in ε (singlets −1/√40, 1/√24; [1,0,1], [0,2,0]: 0; vacuum 1), b-independent; the 36-term SoV sum equals the direct overlap to 10⁻⁴⁴ (60 digits, ε = 10⁻²) and 10⁻⁶⁵ (90 digits, ε = 10⁻³); double precision fails (cond M up to 10²⁵, ⟨0|Ψ⟩/λ₁² ~ ε⁶ for singlets).\n\n**Determinant structure.** K_b = Σ_a τ_a(θ₁−h)P_a(τ₁(θ₂),τ₁(θ₄)) = a 4×4 Casoratian of Q₁,Q₂,Q₃ at θ₁,θ₁−h,θ₁−2h,θ₁−3h bordered by F-site polynomials (exact algebra given the dictionary's D_a form; verified in τ-form on all 256 states, float 7·10⁻¹⁰). Not found (structurally excluded / numerically rejected): a 2×2 pair determinant (pair ranks 4,4,3), a one-row-per-site determinant (site ranks 4), factorised F-site polynomials, a short sum of products (CP rank 7, generic for 4×4×3), a sparse 2603-like global reference (the W^L HW class is dense), a sparser word basis.\n\n**Vandermonde / Cauchy–Binet ansatz (§8b) [exact].** The one-pair F–F formula is exact as written (exchange term γ₂δ₄ρ₂), but det 𝒦 = hρ₂[ρ₂/θ₂₄ − ρ₄/(θ₂₄+h)] is not separable ⇒ no Vandermonde×separable reading and no one-row-per-site determinant; A–A likewise (README {1,3} formula: det = (h/θ₁₃)(1 − ô₁ô₃)); A–F pairs in the cheapest directions factorise (det 𝒦 = 0, no A–F cross factor), but other directions (e.g. site 1 + e₂) create A–F cross terms, so the physical bra has no determinant of the conjectured block form in this language.\n\n**Open.** The right (C-type) SoV basis and non-diagonal measure of the mixed 4/4̄ chain (needed for a GLMR/2603-type bracket determinant; a commuting candidate built from RV's B is not SoV-type); the limit of the measure to the ABJM point; L = 3 pairs. Python scripts and RESULTS.md: `checks/session-2026-10-12/twoblock/`.",
